  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Tax Day for 2026 is Wednesday, April 15, 2026. This is the deadline to file federal income tax returns and pay any taxes owed to the IRS for the 2025 tax year. If you need more time, you can file for an extension by this date to push your filing deadline to October 15, 2026, though any taxes owed are still due on April 15.Key points for Tax Day 2026:Deadline: Returns must be filed or postmarked by April 15, 2026.Extensions: File Form 4868 for an extension, which gives you until October 15, 2026, to file.Payment: Extensions to file are not extensions to pay. Taxes owed must be paid by April 15 to avoid penalties.Special Considerations: Some areas or taxpayers (e.g., in disaster zones or living abroad) may have different deadlines.Would you like to know about filing for an extension, where to file for free, or how to set up a payment plan if you owe taxes?",
